  texts:
  - key: PIO.01.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Pioneer quer dizer pioneira: quem vai primeiro. E o nome n\xE3o \xE9 por acaso."
    enText: 'Pioneer: a word for those who go first. And the name was no accident.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.01.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Mar\xE7o de 1972. Uma pequena sonda, do tamanho de um carro, partiu rumo aos planetas exteriores."
    enText: March 1972. A small probe, no bigger than a car, set out for the outer planets.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.01.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Em menos de 11 horas, cruzou a \xF3rbita da Lua. Ao partir da Terra, era a m\xE1quina mais veloz j\xE1 lan\xE7ada."
    enText: "Within eleven hours it crossed the Moon\u2019s orbit. Leaving Earth, it was the fastest machine ever launched."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.01.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ela gira devagar, como um pi\xE3o. Esse giro ajuda a manter a sonda est\xE1vel na longa viagem."
    enText: It spins slowly, like a top. That steady turning keeps the probe stable on its long journey.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.01.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Longe do Sol, a luz \xE9 fraca. Por isso levava RTGs: geradores que transformam o calor do plut\xF4nio em energia."
    enText: "Far from the Sun, sunlight is faint. So it carried RTGs: generators turning plutonium\u2019s heat into electricity."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Depois de Marte, havia um lugar onde ningu\xE9m tinha passado: o cintur\xE3o de asteroides."
    enText: 'Mars fell behind. Ahead lay a place no one had ever crossed: the asteroid belt.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ningu\xE9m sabia se dava para atravessar. Alguns temiam que uma colis\xE3o encerrasse a miss\xE3o."
    enText: Nobody knew if anything could pass. Some feared a single collision would end the mission.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: 'Imagine o medo: um caminho cheio de pedras, coladas umas nas outras...'
    enText: 'Imagine the fear: a path crowded with rocks, packed close together...'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Na vida real, as pedras ficam muito longe umas das outras. A rota passava a milh\xF5es de km da mais pr\xF3xima."
    enText: In real life, the rocks lie vast distances apart. The route passed millions of kilometres from the nearest.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Os instrumentos procuravam algo bem menor: s\xF3 poeira fina tocou a sonda."
    enText: 'The instruments listened for something far smaller: only fine dust brushed the probe.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.02.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Sete meses depois, a Pioneer saiu do outro lado, inteira. D\xE1 para atravessar o cintur\xE3o!"
    enText: After seven months, Pioneer emerged on the far side, unharmed. The belt could be crossed.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.03.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Novembro de 1973. J\xFApiter, o maior dos planetas, j\xE1 estava \xE0 vista."
    enText: By November 1973, Jupiter, largest of the planets, was in sight.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.03.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Um mundo t\xE3o grande que onze Terras caberiam lado a lado em seu di\xE2metro."
    enText: A world so vast that eleven Earths could stand side by side across its face.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.03.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A Pioneer come\xE7ou a fotografar de longe, a 25 milh\xF5es de quil\xF4metros."
    enText: Pioneer began taking pictures from 25 million kilometres away.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.03.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Mas um comando e sua resposta podiam levar at\xE9 uma hora e meia."
    enText: Yet a command and its reply could take up to an hour and a half.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A Pioneer n\xE3o tinha uma c\xE2mera como a do celular."
    enText: Pioneer had no camera like the one in your phone.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A cada volta, ela via s\xF3 uma linha fina de J\xFApiter, em apenas duas cores: vermelho e azul."
    enText: 'With each turn, it saw just one thin line of Jupiter, in only two colours: red and blue.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Primeiro a luz vermelha: a imagem come\xE7a a aparecer, uma linha de cada vez."
    enText: Red light first, and the picture begins to appear, one line at a time.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ent\xE3o a radia\xE7\xE3o de J\xFApiter disparou comandos indevidos no instrumento."
    enText: "Then Jupiter\u2019s radiation triggered unwanted commands in the instrument."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A equipe enviou sequ\xEAncias de recupera\xE7\xE3o, e a observa\xE7\xE3o continuou."
    enText: The team sent recovery sequences, and the observing carried on.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A Pioneer nunca viu o verde. Os computadores na Terra o estimaram, e J\xFApiter apareceu em cores."
    enText: Pioneer never saw green. Computers on Earth worked it out, and Jupiter appeared in colour.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.07
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Algumas imagens se perderam, inclusive a de Io. Mas muito chegou at\xE9 n\xF3s."
    enText: "Some pictures were lost, Io\u2019s among them. But so much reached us."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.08
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Esta \xE9 Ganimedes, vista pela Pioneer 10 em 1973: fotos de perto da maior lua do Sistema Solar."
    enText: "This is Ganymede, seen by Pioneer 10 in 1973: close-ups of the Solar System\u2019s largest moon."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.04.09
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Eram imagens melhores que qualquer telesc\xF3pio da Terra podia oferecer."
    enText: These pictures were sharper than anything a telescope on Earth could offer.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Mais perto, passou pelas grandes luas de J\xFApiter e fotografou Ganimedes de perto."
    enText: "Closer it came, passing Jupiter\u2019s great moons and photographing Ganymede up close."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "J\xFApiter \xE9 cercado por radia\xE7\xE3o milhares de vezes mais forte que a da Terra."
    enText: "Jupiter is wrapped in radiation thousands of times stronger than Earth\u2019s."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: Absorveu mais de mil vezes a dose fatal a uma pessoa. Surgiram comandos indevidos; havia reservas.
    enText: It absorbed over a thousand times a fatal human dose. Unwanted commands arose; backups were ready.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "4 de dezembro de 1973: a Pioneer 10 foi a primeira a sobrevoar J\xFApiter."
    enText: '4 December 1973: Pioneer 10 became the first to fly past Jupiter.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A cerca de 130.000 km das nuvens: tr\xEAs vezes mais perto que a Lua da Terra."
    enText: 'About 130,000 km above the clouds: three times closer than the Moon to us.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "A gravidade de J\xFApiter curvou seu caminho e deu o impulso para seguir al\xE9m dos planetas."
    enText: "Jupiter\u2019s gravity bent its path and gave it the boost to travel beyond the planets."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.09.07
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Viu que a radia\xE7\xE3o de J\xFApiter era mais forte que o esperado, e isso mudou a Voyager."
    enText: "It found Jupiter\u2019s radiation fiercer than expected, which shaped Voyager\u2019s design."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Depois de J\xFApiter, n\xE3o haveria volta: rumo \xE0s estrelas, a Pioneer levava uma carta numa placa de alum\xEDnio dourado."
    enText: 'No return journey: Pioneer was bound for the stars, carrying a letter on a gold-coloured plaque.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Hidrog\xEAnio, o \xE1tomo mais comum do Universo: a nossa r\xE9gua."
    enText: 'First, hydrogen, the commonest atom in the Universe: our ruler.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: 'Pulsares: estrelas que piscam e mostram onde fica o Sol.'
    enText: Then pulsars, blinking stars that show where the Sun lies.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: 'O Sistema Solar: a sonda saindo do terceiro planeta, a Terra.'
    enText: 'The Solar System: Pioneer leaving the third planet, Earth.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ao lado, o contorno da pr\xF3pria Pioneer, para dar escala."
    enText: "Beside it, Pioneer\u2019s own outline, to show our size."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "E duas figuras. Uma delas acena: ol\xE1!"
    enText: And before it, two figures. One of them is waving hello.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.05.07
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Uma placa de alum\xEDnio dourado: uma carta para um encontro que talvez nunca aconte\xE7a."
    enText: 'A gold-coloured aluminium plaque: a letter for an encounter that may never happen.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Feita para durar 21 meses, a Pioneer continuou: passou a dist\xE2ncia de Saturno em 1976 e a de Urano em 1979."
    enText: "Built to last twenty-one months, Pioneer carried on: it crossed the distance of Saturn\u2019s orbit in 1976 and Uranus\u2019s in 1979."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "13 de junho de 1983: cruzou a dist\xE2ncia da \xF3rbita de Netuno, com os instrumentos ainda funcionando normalmente."
    enText: "13 June 1983: it crossed the distance of Neptune\u2019s orbit, its instruments still working normally."
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ano ap\xF3s ano, os geradores enfraqueciam. Os instrumentos passaram a revezar-se e foram sendo desligados."
    enText: Year by year the generators weakened. The instruments took turns, and one by one were switched off.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Em 1998, a Voyager 1 a ultrapassou e se tornou a m\xE1quina humana mais distante, em outra dire\xE7\xE3o."
    enText: In 1998, Voyager 1 overtook it to become the most distant human-made object, travelling in another direction.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.06.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: A Pioneer havia mostrado o caminho. Agora, a Terra escutava cada vez mais longe.
    enText: Pioneer had shown the way. Now Earth had to listen from ever farther away.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: O sinal estava mais fraco que um sussurro. As antenas da Terra ainda conseguiriam ouvi-lo?
    enText: "Its signal was now fainter than a whisper. Could Earth\u2019s antennas still hear it?"
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Mar\xE7o de 2002. Trinta anos depois do lan\xE7amento, a Pioneer ainda respondia."
    enText: March 2002. Thirty years after launch, Pioneer was still answering.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Abril de 2002. Os \xFAltimos dados de seus instrumentos chegaram \xE0 Terra."
    enText: April 2002. The last data from its instruments reached Earth.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Janeiro de 2003. Um \xFAltimo sinal fraco, de 12 bilh\xF5es de quil\xF4metros, levou mais de 11 horas para chegar."
    enText: January 2003. A last faint signal, from twelve billion kilometres away, took over eleven hours to reach us.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.05
    group: narrative
    ptText: Fevereiro de 2003. A Terra escutou outra vez e nenhum sinal foi detectado.
    enText: February 2003. Earth listened once more, and no signal was detected.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.07.06
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Sem energia suficiente para nos alcan\xE7ar, a Pioneer 10 ficou em sil\xEAncio. Mas n\xE3o parou."
    enText: Without enough power to reach us, Pioneer 10 fell silent. But it did not stop.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.08.01
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Ela segue em dire\xE7\xE3o \xE0 estrela vermelha Aldebaran: uma viagem de milh\xF5es de anos."
    enText: 'It travels on, towards the red star Aldebaran: a journey measured in millions of years.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.08.02
    group: narrative
    ptText: Feita para durar 21 meses, funcionou por mais de 30 anos.
    enText: Built to last twenty-one months, it lasted more than thirty years.
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.08.03
    group: narrative
    ptText: "E o nome n\xE3o foi por acaso: primeira aos planetas exteriores, primeira a cruzar o cintur\xE3o, primeira a sobrevoar J\xFApiter."
    enText: 'And the name was no accident: first to the outer planets, first across the asteroid belt, first to fly past Jupiter.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.08.04
    group: narrative
    ptText: "Pioneer quer dizer pioneira. Toda grande viagem come\xE7a com quem vai primeiro, e a Pioneer 10 foi primeiro, por todos n\xF3s."
    enText: 'Pioneer: one who goes first. Every great journey begins with someone who goes first. Pioneer 10 went first, for us all.'
    ptStatus: derived
    enStatus: derived
  - key: PIO.UI.start
    group: hud
    ptText: "Pioneer 10 \xB7 Abrir caminho"
    enText: "Pioneer 10 \xB7 Going first"
    ptStatus: approved
    enStatus: approved
  - key: PIO.UI.dossier
    group: hud
    ptText: "A primeira visita a J\xFApiter. Transforme sinais em imagens e escute uma viagem de trinta anos."
    enText: The first visit to Jupiter. Turn signals into images and listen to a thirty-year journey.
    ptStatus: approved
    enStatus: approved
